{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: grammar_guided_node_reduction\n\nI need to implement `solve(case)` that:\n1. Takes a payload with `nodes` (a tree) and `required_symbols`\n2. Returns `removed_node_ids` and `retained_node_ids`\n\nRules:\n- Never remove root, a required symbol node, or a node with retained children\n- Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n- Consider deeper nodes before shallower nodes (process deeper first)\n- Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n- Return sorted retained IDs and actual removal order\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build the tree from nodes\n2. Process nodes in order: deeper first, tie-break by node ID (lexicographic? or the order they appear?)\n3. For each candidate (removable=true), try to remove it:\n   - Check that after removal, all required symbols are still represented\n   - Check that removing it doesn't leave children orphaned (actually, if we remove a node, its children would become orphaned - but we should only remove a node if it has no retained children)\n   - Actually: \"Never remove... a node with retained children\" - so a node can only be removed if all its children have already been removed\n\nWait, let me re-read:\n- \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\" - process deeper nodes first\n- \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\"\n- \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\"\n\nSo the algorithm is:\n1. Sort nodes by depth descending, then by node ID for tie-breaking\n2. For each node in that order:\n   - Skip if not removable\n   - Skip if it's root or has a required symbol\n   - Skip if it has retained children (children that haven't been removed yet)\n   - Try removing: check if all required symbols still have at least one node representing them\n   - If yes, mark as removed\n3. Return removed_node_ids (in removal order) and retained_node_ids (sorted)\n\nWait, \"a required symbol\" - does this mean the node's symbol is in required_symbols? Let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo \"a required symbol\" means a node whose symbol is in required_symbols.\n\nAnd \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - this means after removing the node, each symbol in required_symbols must still have at least one remaining node with that symbol.\n\nLet me trace through case 0:\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n- Nodes sorted by depth desc, then node ID:\n\ndepth 2: n4 (removable=true, symbol=s1), n5 (removable=false, symbol=s2), n6 (removable=true, symbol=s0)\ndepth 1: n1 (removable=false, symbol=s1), n2 (removable=true, symbol=s2), n3 (removable=false, symbol=s0)\ndepth 0: root (removable=false, symbol=root)\n\nSort by depth desc, then node ID:\n- depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID: n4, n5, n6)\n- depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth 0: root\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1):\n- Not root ✓\n- symbol s1 is in required_symbols - so we can't remove it? \n\nWait, \"Never remove... a required symbol\" - this means if the node's symbol is in required_symbols, we can't remove it. So n4 with symbol=s1 cannot be removed.\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, removable=false): skip (not removable)\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0):\n- Not root ✓\n- symbol s0 not in required_symbols ✓\n- No children (it's at depth 2 and has no children in the list) ✓\n- After removal, check required symbols still represented:\n  - \"root\": root node still there ✓\n  - \"s1\": n1 (s1) and n4 (s1) still there ✓\n- Remove n6 ✓\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, removable=false): skip\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2):\n- Not root ✓\n- symbol s2 not in required_symbols ✓\n- Check children: n4 is a child of n2. Is n4 retained? Yes (n4 was not removed). So n2 has retained children - cannot remove.\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, removable=false): skip\n\nProcess root (removable=false): skip\n\nSo:\n- removed: [n6]\n- retained: [root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5] sorted\n\nLet me check the tie-breaking for node IDs. The IDs are strings like \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", etc. Lexicographic sorting:\n- \"n1\" \u003c \"n2\" \u003c \"n3\" \u003c \"n4\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"n6\" \u003c \"root\" (lexicographic: 'n' \u003c 'r')\n\nWait, actually lexicographic: 'n' has ASCII 110, 'r' has ASCII 114. So \"n...\" \u003c \"r...\"\n\nDepth 2 nodes: n4, n5, n6 → sorted by ID: n4, n5, n6 ✓\nDepth 1 nodes: n1, n2, n3 → sorted by ID: n1, n2, n3 ✓\nDepth 0: root\n\nSo the candidate order is: n4, n5, n6, n1, n2, n3, root\n\nThis seems right for case 0.\n\nNow let me think about the \"retained_node_ids\" output - it says \"sorted\". Sorted how? Probably lexicographically by ID, or by depth? The schema says just array of strings. I'll sort lexicographically.\n\nActually wait - let me re-read the output contract: \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\"\n\nSo retained_node_ids should be sorted (probably alphabetically), and removed_node_ids should be in the order they were actually removed.\n\nLet me now write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"nodes must be a list\")\n    if not isinstance(case[\"required_symbols\"], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"required_symbols must be a list\")\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    node_by_id = {}\n    for node in nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        if nid in node_by_id:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Duplicate node id: {nid}\")\n        node_by_id[nid] = node\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_by_id}\n    for node in nodes:\n        parent = node[\"parent\"]\n        if parent is not None:\n            if parent not in node_by_id:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {parent} not found\")\n            children[parent].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Sort candidate order: deeper first, tie-break by node ID (lexicographic)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    # Track removed nodes\n    removed = set()\n    removal_order = []\n    \n    # Count symbols in retained nodes\n    symbol_counts = {}\n    for node in nodes:\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove root (parent is None)\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is required\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove a node with retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c not in removed for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if all required symbols remain represented after removal\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in required_symbols:\n            # Already handled above\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentative removal: check required symbols still covered\n        can_remove = True\n        # The node being removed contributes its symbol. Check if symbol_counts[sym] \u003e 1 or sym not required\n        # Actually we already checked sym not in required_symbols, so this is fine\n        # But wait - we need to check that after removal, required symbols are still represented\n        # Since sym is not in required_symbols, removing this node doesn't affect required symbol coverage\n        # So we can always remove it if the other conditions are met?\n        \n        # Wait, let me re-read: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\"\n        # The required symbols check is about the entire set of remaining nodes, not just this node's symbol.\n        # But since we've already ensured the node's own symbol isn't required, removing it can only affect\n        # coverage of its own symbol. All other required symbols are unaffected.\n        # So the condition is automatically satisfied when symbol is not in required_symbols.\n        \n        # Remove the node\n        removed.add(nid)\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n        symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\n    \n    retained = sorted([n[\"id\"] for n in nodes if n[\"id\"] not in removed])\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained\n    }\n```\n\nWait, but what about the \"root\" check? The root node has `\"parent\": null`. But we also check `removable=False` for root in the fixture. The rule says \"Never remove the root\" - we should check by parent=None.\n\nAlso, I need to think more carefully about the case where a required symbol node could be the last representative of a required symbol. But we skip required symbol nodes directly.\n\nActually wait - I need to reconsider. \"Never remove a required symbol\" - does this mean:\n(a) Never remove a node whose symbol is a required symbol, OR\n(b) Never remove a node such that its removal would eliminate all nodes with a required symbol?\n\nI initially interpreted it as (a). But \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" suggests (b) is also checked separately. So maybe interpretation is:\n- \"Never remove a required symbol\" means never remove a node whose symbol is in required_symbols\n- Additionally, also check that all required symbols remain represented (which would be an extra check)\n\nGiven the two conditions overlap (if we never remove nodes with required symbols, required symbol coverage is maintained for those symbols), the \"tentatively remove\" check would be redundant in most cases. But maybe there are edge cases...\n\nActually, I think the \"never remove a required symbol\" rule refers to node-level exclusion, and the \"tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\" is a broader check. Let me keep both checks to be safe, but since a node with a required symbol won't be removed (first check), the second check effectively only matters for the symbol counts.\n\nHmm, but given the structure - if a node's symbol is not in required_symbols, removing it can't affect coverage of required symbols. So the tentative check is always satisfied for nodes with non-required symbols.\n\nUnless... the interpretation is different. Maybe \"a required symbol\" in \"Never remove... a required symbol\" doesn't mean the node's symbol. Let me re-read:\n\n\"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nI think \"a required symbol\" here means \"a node that represents a required symbol\" - i.e., a node whose symbol field is in required_symbols. This is consistent with interpretation (a).\n\nAnd \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - this is saying: before confirming the removal, verify that after the tentative removal, all required symbols still have at least one node remaining. This is a separate check from just \"don't remove nodes with required symbols\".\n\nConsider a case where there's only one node with symbol \"s1\" and \"s1\" is required. That node has `removable=false`, so it wouldn't be removed anyway. But what if it had `removable=true`? Then the \"never remove a required symbol\" rule covers it. So they do overlap.\n\nI think my implementation is correct. Let me trace through case 0 again more carefully:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root, parent=null\n- n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1, parent=root\n- n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2, parent=root\n- n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0, parent=root\n- n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols: {root, s1}\n\nchildren:\n- root: [n1, n2, n3]\n- n1: [n6]\n- n2: [n4]\n- n3: [n5]\n- n4: []\n- n5: []\n- n6: []\n\nsorted_nodes (by -depth, then id):\ndepth 2: n4, n5, n6\ndepth 1: n1, n2, n3\ndepth 0: root\n\nProcess n4: removable=true, parent=n2 (not null), symbol=s1 (in required_symbols) → SKIP\n\nProcess n5: removable=false → SKIP\n\nProcess n6: removable=true, parent=n1 (not null), symbol=s0 (not in required_symbols), children=[] (no retained children)\n- Can remove. Remove n6.\n- removed = {n6}, removal_order = [n6]\n\nProcess n1: removable=false → SKIP\n\nProcess n2: removable=true, parent=root (not null), symbol=s2 (not in required_symbols)\n- children of n2: [n4]. Is n4 in removed? No → has retained children → SKIP\n\nProcess n3: removable=false → SKIP\n\nProcess root: removable=false → SKIP\n\nResult:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n6\"]\n- retained_node_ids: sorted([\"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\"]) = [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nWait, lexicographic sort of [\"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\"]:\n- \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\" all start with 'n' (ASCII 110)\n- \"root\" starts with 'r' (ASCII 114)\n- 'n' \u003c 'r', so all n-prefixed come before root\n- Result: [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nThat seems reasonable. Let me verify case 1 quickly:\n\nCase 1 nodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root\n- n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1\n- n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2\n- n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0\n- n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols: {root, s1}\n\nSame structure as case 0. Same result expected:\n- n4: symbol=s1 → SKIP\n- n5: not removable → SKIP\n- n6: removable, symbol=s0, no children → REMOVE\n- n1: not removable → SKIP\n- n2: has retained child n4 → SKIP\n- n3: not removable → SKIP\n- root: not removable → SKIP\n\nResult: removed=[n6], retained=[n1,n2,n3,n4,n5,root]\n\nCase 2 is also the same structure.\n\nAll three cases look like they'd produce the same pattern. The utility values don't seem to be used? Let me re-read the task...\n\n\"grammar_guided_node_reduction\" - the task is about Perses syntax-guided reduction. The utility field might not be directly used in the algorithm as described. The algorithm is:\n1. Process nodes deeper-first\n2. Try to remove each removable node if it doesn't violate constraints\n\nThe utility might be for a different interpretation... but the artifact says \"Use only quantities present in the case payload\" and \"Never depend on hash-map iteration\". The core algorithm as described doesn't use utility for the removal decision - it's a constraint-based reduction.\n\nWait, could utility be used for ranking within the same depth? \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\" - so at equal depth, we sort by node ID. Utility is not used as a tie-breaker. Good.\n\nLet me finalize the implementation. I need to handle validation too.\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate structure\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"nodes must be a non-empty list\")\n    \n    node_by_id = {}\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in (\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"):\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing field: {field}\")\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        if nid in node_by_id:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Duplicate node id: {nid}\")\n        node_by_id[nid] = node\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_by_id}\n    root_count = 0\n    for node in nodes:\n        parent = node[\"parent\"]\n        if parent is None:\n            root_count += 1\n        else:\n            if parent not in node_by_id:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {parent} not found for node {node['id']}\")\n            children[parent].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    if root_count != 1:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Expected exactly one root node, found {root_count}\")\n    \n    # Sort: deeper first, tie-break by node ID (lexicographic)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removed = set()\n    removal_order = []\n    \n    # Track symbol coverage\n    symbol_counts = {}\n    for node in nodes:\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue  # Never remove root\n        \n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue  # Never remove a required symbol\n        \n        # Never remove a node with retained children\n        if any(c not in removed for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentative check: all required symbols remain represented\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        # Since sym is not in required_symbols, removing it won't affect required symbol coverage\n        # This check is always True here, but included for correctness\n        can_remove = True\n        for req_sym in required_symbols:\n            count = symbol_counts.get(req_sym, 0)\n            adjustment = 1 if req_sym == sym else 0\n            if count - adjustment \u003c 1:\n                can_remove = False\n                break\n        \n        if not can_remove:\n            continue\n        \n        removed.add(nid)\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n        symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\n    \n    retained = sorted(nid for nid in node_by_id if nid not in removed)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me double-check the output format matches the schema:\n- `removed_node_ids`: array of strings ✓\n- `retained_node_ids`: array of strings ✓\n- Both required ✓\n- No additional properties ✓\n\nNow I need to encode this as a JSON string in the implementation key.\n\nThe response format should be:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n```\n\nLet me write out the final JSON.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes must be a non-empty list\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"], list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"required_symbols must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    node_by_id = {}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        for field in (\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"):\\n            if field not in node:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Node missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n        if nid in node_by_id:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Duplicate node id: {nid}\\\")\\n        node_by_id[nid] = node\\n\\n    children = {nid: [] for nid in node_by_id}\\n    root_count = 0\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        parent = node[\\\"parent\\\"]\\n        if parent is None:\\n            root_count += 1\\n        else:\\n            if parent not in node_by_id:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent '{parent}' not found for node '{node['id']}'\\\")\\n            children[parent].append(node[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    if root_count != 1:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"Expected exactly one root node, found {root_count}\\\")\\n\\n    # Process deeper nodes first; stable tie-break by node ID (lexicographic)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removed = set()\\n    removal_order = []\\n\\n    # Track symbol counts for required-symbol coverage check\\n    symbol_counts = {}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        sym = node[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be marked removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove root (parent is None)\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is a required symbol\\n        if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(child not in removed for child in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentative check: all required symbols remain represented after removal\\n        sym = node[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        can_remove = True\\n        for req_sym in required_symbols:\\n            current_count = symbol_counts.get(req_sym, 0)\\n            decrement = 1 if req_sym == sym else 0\\n            if current_count - decrement \u003c 1:\\n                can_remove = False\\n                break\\n\\n        if not can_remove:\\n            continue\\n\\n        removed.add(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n        symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\\n\\n    retained = sorted(nid for nid in node_by_id if nid not in removed)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01gGrmtiz4ndVWzvLmBkxj2R","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2539,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":51,"output_tokens":5848,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5015},"service_tier":"standard"}}